      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/24-mullets/rhinomugil-corsula-en/",
      "html": "<p>The Indian Four Eyed Fish belongs to the mullet family. It usually grows to 15-20 cm, on rare occasions up to 45 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/24-mullets/rhinomugil-corsula-en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: India.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/24-mullets/rhinomugil-corsula-en/",
      "html": "<p>As in the South American Four Eyes (Anableps), the eyes of Rhinomugil are divided horizontally. Nevertheless, the two genera are not related to each other. With the upper half of the eye the fish can see sharply above the water surface, with the lower part under water.</p>"
    }
